@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: AUTHOR A PRICING ENGINE CONFIGURATION</b>
  --
  {#
    Step | What it carries
    1 | name it, say what it is for, and choose where to start
    2 | choose the products
    3 | choose the model and the engine
    4 | set the parameters
    5 | check it against what the reports need
    6 | review and submit (final)
  }
  --
  <b>STEP 1 - WHAT IS IT FOR</b>
  A party holds few official configurations. A configuration made here starts as a draft.
  { (X) A draft to try a change. No official report can bind it. }
  { ( ) A candidate for the official End of day configuration }
  { ( ) A candidate for the official Intraday configuration }
  --
  <b>STEP 5 - CHECK IT</b>
  A report needs a price for every product type in its portfolio.
  Coverage: 9 of the 11 product types the end of day reports need have a row.
  Not covered: CreditDefaultSwap, EquityOption.
  --
  <b>STEP 6 - REVIEW AND SUBMIT</b>
  [ Back ] | [ Save as draft ] | [ Submit for sign-off ]
  Submit is not offered while a needed product type has no row.
}

@enduml
